{
 "issue": 44,
 "title": "Refit on train plus validation with a fixed tree count and epoch schedule, measured by a four year backtest inside 1995 to 2020, XGBoost and GRU, 1 hour",
 "result": "no-gain",
 "result_note": "label by the retrain policy bar against A (mean of 3 seeds): XGBoost B changes overall MSE by +0.03% (95% -0.24 .. +0.30) and B2 by -0.26% (-0.54 .. +0.02); GRU B by -0.25% (-0.75 .. +0.21) and B2 by +0.01% (-0.40 .. +0.39). Storm hour changes are within -0.4 .. +0.3% with intervals spanning zero. Far from the 2% overall or 3% storm bar, so refitting on more recent years with the inner tree and epoch counts gives no measurable gain. The optimistic production reference P (early stopped on the scored years) is 0.64% lower in overall MSE than A for XGBoost.",
 "date": "2026-11-27",
 "split": "validation only. Fit and early stopping years end before 2017-01-01; 2017-01-01 .. 2020-12-31 is only scored. The table was cut after 2021-01-01 00:00, used only as the target of the last validation hour, so no test row existed in either run (XGBoost fit(..., test=False), GRU backtest_parts).",
 "horizon_hours": 1,
 "configuration": {
  "A": "current protocol shifted four years back: fit 1995 .. 2012, early stopping on 2013 .. 2016 (scripts/train_xgb.py --backtest-shift 4, scripts/train_gru.py --backtest-shift 4); GRU scaling statistics and target scale from 1995 .. 2012 only. Trees kept: best_iteration + 1; GRU: best epoch and the epochs after which ReduceLROnPlateau halved the learning rate",
  "B": "refit: fit 1995 .. 2016 with exactly A's tree count per seed (--fixed-trees N), GRU exactly A's best epoch count per seed with A's learning rate halvings before that epoch replayed (--fixed-epochs N --lr-drops ...), no early stopping, no look at 2017 .. 2020",
  "B2": "as B with round(1.2 x) the trees and epochs; the GRU halving epochs are stretched by 1.2 as well",
  "P": "optimistic reference only, not a candidate: the production protocol, fit 1995 .. 2016 and early stopped on 2017 .. 2020, the hours it is scored on. XGBoost: rerun here, seed 0 reproduces 2151 trees and validation RMSE 2.6565 of reports/xgb_baseline.json. GRU: not rerun, the mean of 3 seeds from validation_scores in reports/gru_baseline.json (no paired interval)",
  "C": "optional recency weighting variant of the issue not run; the assignment lists A, B and B2",
  "params": "XGBoost PARAMS of scripts/train_xgb.py (89 features, 6 lags, storm weight 1), GRU constants of scripts/train_gru.py (hidden 64, batch 512, lr 0.002, max 40 epochs, patience 6)",
